From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: michael moore <mrmoore27@pm.me>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 09:02:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 23/27] gateway, pool: lazarus-gateway enrol and the public
 enrol route
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

lazarus-gateway --config … enrol prints SOV-P-002 §4's LZT1 register v1|v2 from the gateway's
persisted identity key (never a new one), at the node's tip, with G's signature and the JSON
body the site takes; v2 needs --payout and leaves the payout signature to the wallet.

pool/server.py: POST /api/sovereignty/enrol rate-limits per client IP and per G (every attempt
counts), bounds the body to 8 KB, forwards only the fields primed reads to its loopback
/sovereignty/enrol with the local token, and answers 503 when enrolment is shut (mode off, no
token). The client is CF-Connecting-IP or the first X-Forwarded-For hop only from a trusted
proxy. Nothing here stores or returns node addresses.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
