 | `observe` | Job snapshots, attestations and blocks are recorded. The detector runs in the background every `sovereignty-recompute-secs` (default 300) on a copy of its store, never under the ledger lock; stats.json and `GET /sovereignty.json` serve the last pass (`compute_ms`, `computed_at`), with `published: false`. |
 | `publish` | As `observe`, with `published: true` for the pool site. |
 
-`POST /sovereignty/{register,attest,canary}` need the mode on and the token from
-`data-dir/sovereignty.token` in an `X-Sovereignty-Token` header; the other POSTs (snapshot,
-check, credit, observe, apply-bonus) also need `sovereignty-demo = true` (local rnd only).
-
-**Canary evidence comes from canary checks (SOV-P-002 W8).** The canary sidecar
-(`lazarus/canary/`, W9) reports each canary it places with `POST /sovereignty/canary`
-`{"gateway": G, "t": <delivered, unix s>, "txid": <hex>, "kind": "own"|"shared"|"decoy"}`.
-An own canary schedules one extra check of that gateway `sovereignty-canary-check-secs`
-(default 45) later: on its next 5 s tick the session sends `request_full_block` for the newest
-job the gateway has sent (whatever its shares scored). The reply counts only if its transactions hash to that job's merkle branches, so a
-gateway cannot answer with a list its miners are not hashing (refusals are logged and counted
-in `/sovereignty.json` `store.checks_refused`). A canary is judged by the checks of jobs Prime
-first saw 12–180 s after its delivery, and hit if one of them holds it; shared canaries and
-decoys are read from the same job lists. Job snapshots still feed the timing and cluster
-features but are no canary evidence. One gateway gets at most one canary check per
-`sovereignty-canary-check-gap-secs` (default 300: a full block is megabytes of upload for it);
-checks due together are made once. 256 checks are kept per key.
+`POST /sovereignty/{enrol,attest}` need the mode on and the token from
+`data-dir/sovereignty.token` in an `X-Sovereignty-Token` header; the other POSTs (the old
+`register`, snapshot, canary, credit, observe, apply-bonus) also need `sovereignty-demo = true`
+(local rnd only).
+
+**Registration** (`POST /sovereignty/enrol`, SOV-P-002 §4; public through `pool/server.py`'s
+rate-limited `POST /api/sovereignty/enrol`). `lazarus-gateway --config … enrol [--version v2
+--payout ADDR] [--node host:port]` prints the message from the gateway's persisted identity key:
+
+```
+LZT1 register v1|v2
+pool: lazarus-xbt
+chain: XBT
+G: <64 hex>
+node: <host:port | xxx.onion:port | none>
+tag: <≤ 32 chars>
+at: <height> <block hash>
+payout: <address>          (v2 only, last line)
+```
+
+Body `{"message", "g_sig", "payout_sig"?, "proof"?: "bip322"|"signmessage"|"spend",
+"spend_txid"?, "spend_block"?}`. `g_sig` is ed25519 by `G` over
+`"XBT-SOVEREIGN-TIDES/register\0" ‖ message`. `at` must be one of the pool node's last 144
+blocks and newer than the key's last accepted message. v2's payout proof: BIP322 simple or full
+(`datum_wire::bip322`; 0x21 `UnifiedSighash` signatures only with the `unified-sighash` feature),
+`signmessage` for a P2PKH payout (the node's `verifymessage`), or a confirmed tx from the payout
+to itself with `OP_RETURN "LZT1E" ‖ SHA256(message)[0..16]`. The payout must match
+`gateway-scripts.json`, or the gateway's first split coinbase confirms it (paying elsewhere
+refuses the key). A new `G` from the same payout supersedes the old one for good; `LZT1 revoke v2`
+(lines `pool`, `chain`, `G`, `payout`, `at`), signed by the payout, ends a binding. Key age
+(`sovereignty-min-key-age-secs`) counts from the first v2's `at` block.
 `sovereignty-bonus` pays nothing unless the mode is on. `authored` and `directory` (payout
 addresses) appear in the report only with the bonus on; node addresses never do.
 
